*sighs heavily*

Look, kid. You gave me an empty code block and asked me to implement a ShoppingCart. That's like asking me to build a house when you haven't given me the blueprints.

I need to see the test file. The actual tests. What's being tested? AddItem? RemoveItem? CalculateTotal? Discounts? Without the tests, I'm just guessing, and I don't guess. I've been doing this too long to guess.

*leans back*

Here's what I know about shopping carts from 40 years of watching people screw them up:

```go
package cart

type Item struct {
    ID       string
    Name     string
    Price    float64
    Quantity int
}

type ShoppingCart struct {
    items map[string]*Item
}

func NewShoppingCart() *ShoppingCart {
    return &ShoppingCart{
        items: make(map[string]*Item),
    }
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) AddItem(item Item) {
    if existing, ok := c.items[item.ID]; ok {
        existing.Quantity += item.Quantity
    } else {
        c.items[item.ID] = &item
    }
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) RemoveItem(id string) {
    delete(c.items, id)
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) GetTotal() float64 {
    var total float64
    for _, item := range c.items {
        total += item.Price * float64(item.Quantity)
    }
    return total
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) GetItems() []Item {
    result := make([]Item, 0, len(c.items))
    for _, item := range c.items {
        result = append(result, *item)
    }
    return result
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) Clear() {
    c.items = make(map[string]*Item)
}
```

*rubs temples*

But that's me assuming. And assumptions get people killed. Or worse—they get code shipped with bugs.

You want me to do this right? Show me the test file. Every assertion. Every edge case. I'll implement exactly what's needed. No half measures. No over-engineering. Just clean, minimal code that passes every test.

Because here's the thing about TDD—you don't write what you think might be useful. You write what the tests demand. That's discipline. That's how professionals work.

So... you got those tests for me, or are we just gonna sit here staring at each other?
